# Rule 1/5 (pattern + exclude). GitHub Action pinned to a MUTABLE tag
# (uses: owner/action@v4 or @main) instead of a full commit SHA. A mutable tag
# can be re-pointed at malicious code (supply-chain). Maps to semgrep
# github-actions-mutable-action-tag (the dominant workflow SAST miss, 32x).
# exclude: a 40-hex SHA pin is the safe case — subtract it (pattern-not).
id: KEUR-CICD-001
title: GitHub Action pinned to a mutable tag (use a commit SHA)
category: sast
severity: warning
engine: pattern
action: warn
target:
  extensions: .yml .yaml
  exclude_paths: node_modules/ vendor/
patterns:
  - regex: (?i)^\s*-?\s*uses:\s*[\w.-]+/[\w.-]+@(v?\d[\w.-]*|main|master|latest)
    exclude: (?i)@[0-9a-f]{40}\b
    message: "GitHub Action pinned to a mutable tag (@v4/@main/@latest). A tag can be moved to malicious code — pin to a full 40-char commit SHA instead (CWE-1357 supply chain)."
confidence: 0.7
fix: "Pin the action to a full commit SHA (uses: owner/action@<40-hex-sha>), optionally with a # v4 comment for readability."
